<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trepča</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trepča is a mining area near Mitrovica in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a>, worked for lead, zinc and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> its silver mines, operated with the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> miners and Ragusan merchants, were a major source of revenue for Serbian rulers. The Trepča mining complex later became one of the largest industrial enterprises of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>.</p></div>
